    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d143">

                <pb facs="0137" n="123" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg123"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.51 Frozen Credits/5217: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-01-29T15:00:00-04:00">January 29, 1942—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:57 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>178. Your circular telegram January 24, 4 p.m.<anchor n="74" xml:id="d143-f1"/>
                    No freezing control measures have been instituted. Chilean Government was
                    informed my note December 19 that we would like to see prompt adoption measures
                    numbered 1, 3, 4 and 5 of Department’s telegram December 15, 10 p.m.,<anchor
                        n="75" xml:id="d143-f2"/> but so far as can be learned here no action in
                    this connection is contemplated at this juncture.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d143-f1" n="74" xml:id="d143-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it requested information as to what control measures had been
                    instituted (840.51 Frozen Credits/5168a).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d143-f2" n="75" xml:id="d143-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; in this telegram the Department expressed the desire that the
                    American Republics prevent or curb business transactions with the Axis and
                    indicated the measures desirable to freeze the business operations of
                    individuals, banks and other companies having Axis connections (840.51 Frozen
                    Credits/4686a).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
